==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Castaway Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Seafarer Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This unit is extremely good at controlling close-ranged Alien enemies. Protect him well to ensure that the Aliens stay frozen in their tracks while your [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cats]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]], and [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cats]] wipe out the frozen enemies.

Due to having acceptable stats as a short-ranged area attacker, it is possible to stack several of them over a long period of time to effectively keep some Alien enemies stunlocked. This is possible against some powerful Alien bosses such as [[Corrupted Valkyrie]] and [[Cosmic Cyclone]] making the fight against them much easier. Aside from this, it can be used effectively as a generalist midranger early on thanks to these stats and survive.

==='''True Form'''===
Seafarer Cat is a notable improvement on Surfer Cat thanks to his better stats, [[Freeze|Freeze]] and guaranteed [[Survive|Survive]] ability. With these, he can be stacked much more easily and effectively, even when enemies push through meatshields, becoming a much better generalist as a result.

==='''Talents'''===
Since this Cat has great stats, improving his health and damage is a good use of NP, as long as Seafarer is also granted a high level. The improvement to his freezing capabilities is also a nice talent, as it makes this unit more consistent and way better when stacked against aliens that don't outrange him. Warp immune has advantages and disadvantages. Unlock it for better performance against nasty backliners with warp, or don't, for better survivability in rare occasions. Lastly, avoid Curse Resist, as the stages where it would even matter are few.

